    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d738">

                <pb facs="0862" n="850" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg850"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115A Pacific War/218: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bern</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-13"
                            >August 13, 1942</date>.<lb/>[Received August 13—4:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3736. American interests—Philippines. Legation’s 3686, August 10.<anchor n="97"
                        xml:id="d738-f1"/> Intercroixrouge states Japanese authorities gave
                    following information to Intercroixrouge’s representative Tokyo regarding
                    Philippines: “Prisoners of war and civilian internees under good conditions.
                    Internment camp Santo Tomas, Manila, large and well organized. Sanitary, food
                    and clothing situation prisoners and internees good.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d738-f1" n="97" xml:id="d738-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported that International Red Cross efforts to send a
                    delegation to the Philippines had failed (740.00115A Pacific War/213).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
